<title>SINGAPORE: Sato Kogyo jv wins S$166.4 mln subway deal.</title>
<headline>Sato Kogyo jv wins S$166.4 mln subway deal.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>A joint venture between Sato Kogyo Company Ltd and Hock Lian Seng Engineering Pte Ltd won a S$166.38 million Singapore government contract to construct and design a subway.</p>
<p>The deal involves the construction of two underground stations and 1.6 km tunnels linking the two stations along with another 1.2 km going into the depot, a Land Transport Authority statement said.  </p>
<p>It said a second contract, valued at S$311.56 million, for another subway line had been awarded to the joint venture of South Korea's Hyundai Engineering &amp; Construction Co Ltd and Zublin AG of Germany.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
